      content:
          '**Vitals**: BP 134/82 mmHg, HR 78 bpm, RR 16, SpO2 97% via tracheostomy on RA, Temp 36.9C, BMI 22.1.\n\n**General**: Thin male with permanent tracheostomy and HME device in place. Communicates via whiteboard. Appears withdrawn with flat affect.\n\n**Head and Neck**:\n- **Tracheostomy**: Permanent end stoma, well-healed, patent. HME in place. No peristomal skin breakdown.\n- **Neck**: Significant radiation fibrosis — woody, non-pliable tissue throughout anterior and lateral neck bilaterally. Bilateral neck dissection scars well-healed. Limited cervical ROM: flexion 30 degrees, extension 20 degrees, rotation 30 degrees bilaterally.\n- **Oral**: Xerostomia with thick ropey saliva. Trismus with interincisal distance 22 mm (normal >40 mm). Oral mucosa atrophic with radiation changes. No visible fistula.\n- **TEP Site**: Tracheoesophageal puncture site patent, prosthesis in place. No leakage around prosthesis noted.\n\n**Right Shoulder/Upper Extremity**:\n- **Inspection**: Right scapular winging prominent. Right trapezius visibly atrophied compared to left.\n- **ROM**: Right shoulder — active flexion 85 degrees, passive 140 degrees; active abduction 70 degrees, passive 130 degrees. Left shoulder full ROM.\n- **Strength**: Right upper trapezius 2/5, right middle trapezius 3-/5, right lower trapezius 3/5. Right deltoid 4/5, right serratus anterior 4/5. Left upper extremity 5/5 throughout.\n- **Special Tests**: Positive scapular winging with forward flexion. Pain with right shoulder active abduction 60-90 degrees.\n\n**Neurologic**: CN XI (spinal accessory) — right trapezius and SCM weakness. Remaining cranial nerves grossly intact. Hearing diminished bilaterally (unable to hear whispered voice at 2 feet). Peripheral sensation intact.\n\n**Respiratory**: Breathing comfortably through tracheostomy. Lungs clear to auscultation. Peak cough flow reduced secondary to laryngectomy (loss of glottic closure for effective cough).',
